    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36362" root="قوت" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَائِتٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَاتَ</span>; <i>Feeding,</i> &amp;c. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And hence, <i>Sufficing</i>]. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">القَائِتُ مِنَ العَيْشِ</span> means
<i>What is sufficient</i> [<i>of the means of subsistence</i>].
(K.) And one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ فِى قَائِتٍ مِنَ العَيْشِ</span> <i>He
is in a state of sufficiency</i> [<i>in respect of the means
of subsistence</i>]. (S. O.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُوتٌ</span>, in
two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also 8, former half. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">القَائِتُ</span>
is an appellation of <i>The lion.</i> (O, K.)

